--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/integration/swift-restored-phoenix/REPLAY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Swift client against restored Phoenix rollback
+
+This fixture is for public Mixer revision
+`5fd075d6df49ccf2b2e4699a7bc2e59c7b3fd2e8`. It builds and runs on macOS
+with Xcode, Swift, a Rust toolchain, Elixir 1.20.4 and PostgreSQL 17. The
+iOS runtime identity is synthetic. It needs neither a device nor account
+credentials. All service listeners bind to IPv4 loopback. The browser
+fixture provides a test issuer and OAuth bearer for the stock CLI.
+
+The checked-in receipt records the verified portion through restored
+Phoenix's sequence-2 delivery. The restored-target validation call in
+this patch was added after the bounded run. The rollback, worker, restarted
+Phoenix fetch and offline selection still need executable verification.
+
+From the Mixer checkout, prepare one new owned scratch directory and apply the
+patch to the pinned source export.
+
+```sh
+umask 077
+mkdir -p verification/local
+run=$(mktemp -d "$PWD/verification/local/swift-restored-ios.XXXXXXXX")
+mkdir -p "$run"/{tree,tmp,mix,hex,cargo,swift-cache/repositories,logs,lib}
